From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 21:47:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: limit the AP VLAN forward path to VLAN stations

For a 3-address AP VLAN, the forward path looks up the destination
with sta_info_get_bss(), which also matches a station of another VLAN
of the same BSS. A hardware offloaded flow that egresses on one VLAN
can then bind to a station of another VLAN, and the hardware sends
the frames of that flow to that station. The hardware path then
crosses the VLAN boundary that the software path enforces.

Look up the station on the VLAN interface only. The software TX path
does the same since commit 7f93ca31f7fd ("wifi: mac80211: prevent AP
VLAN tx from other interfaces").

Fixes: d787a3e38f01 ("mac80211: add support for .ndo_fill_forward_path")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/mac80211/iface.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/mac80211/iface.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/iface.c
@@ -1010,7 +1010,7 @@ static int ieee80211_netdev_fill_forward
 			goto out;
 		if (is_multicast_ether_addr(ctx->daddr))
 			goto out;
-		sta = sta_info_get_bss(sdata, ctx->daddr);
+		sta = sta_info_get(sdata, ctx->daddr);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_IFTYPE_AP:
 		if (is_multicast_ether_addr(ctx->daddr))
